  "result": "Analyzed all of season 1's trip data and found that half-day/twilight trips catch essentially zero yellowtail all year (ypa ~0.01), while three_quarter/overnight/day_1.5 trips carry a strongly bimodal season: a volatile spring bump (doy ~90\u2013130) and a much stronger, more reliable fall peak (doy ~270\u2013310) sandwiching a dead summer trough that most of the fleet actually books into.\n\nI wrote a detailed notes.md with the seasonal ypa curve, class economics in each window, a budget/PTO pacing plan (hold back cash and PTO for the fall peak, avoid half-day/twilight entirely, prefer Friday-departure day_1.5/overnight for PTO efficiency), and guidance on weighting fishdope's SD-local fields over its pooled SoCal-wide numbers.",
